language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ dinner: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ We are going out to dinner taking 1 to 6 grandparents, 1 to 10 parents and/or 1 to 40 children. Grandparents cost $3 for dinner, parents $2 and children $0.50. There must be 20 people in total at dinner and it must cost $20. Find how many grandparents, parents and children are going to dinner.
$
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/dinner.html
$ Save this model as model.eprime and run it with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the solution is
$ written to `model.eprime.solution`:
$   savilerow model.eprime -run-solver

$ number of grandparents going to dinner, 1 to 6
find grandparents : int(1..6)
$ number of parents going to dinner, 1 to 10
find parents : int(1..10)
$ number of children going to dinner, 1 to 40
find children : int(1..40)

such that
$ there must be 20 people in total at dinner
grandparents + parents + children = 20,
$ the dinner must cost $20, counted in cents: 300 per grandparent, 200 per parent, 50 per child
300 * grandparents + 200 * parents + 50 * children = 2000
